body:
This pull request integrates the features developed for the "Federated Scaling" project into xFFL. More specifically:

- It integrates federated learning (FL) as a distributed training strategy into xFFL;
- It enables custom splitting of the available processes into federated groups, both symmetric (all federated groups have an equal number of processes) and asymmetric (different federated groups have different numbers of processes);
- It implements an optimised communication pattern to enable minimised communication between federated groups, exchanging at maximum O(size(model));
- It offers a collection of highly optimised aggregation strategies (intra-silo aggregation: layer-wise, bucket-wise, coalesced);
- It integrates Federated Scaling features with PyTorch's FSDP/HSDP, offering full interoperability;
- It implements a preliminary version of a network-aware Federated Scaling training, modelling the federated groups according to the underlying interconnect topology;
- Offers an improved configuration logic, providing default values for the arguments not provided by the user.

This pull request brings a totally new implementation of xFFL, radically changing its usage and potentiality.
Major feature:
-  New, revised command line interface with multiple sub-commands;
- The xFFL CLI now wraps streamFlow, and thus its use is transparent to the user;
- StreamFlow and CWL configurations are now generated interactively with the user;
- New simulation features allow testing a deployment on a facility before running it through StreamFlow.
